cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the archived release."
type: software
title: "InverseCSS: synthetic employer data from published government tables (Maryland pilot, 2021-2024)"
authors:
  - family-names: Hao
    given-names: Lingxin
    affiliation: Johns Hopkins University
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-11-13
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24209077
abstract: >-
  Code that builds synthetic county x six-digit industry x ownership x quarter employer
  groups for Maryland, 2021-2024, from published BLS QCEW and Census QWI tables: suppressed
  cells are imputed with Dirichlet-multinomial draws within published totals and raked
  to state totals in the same draw, in M = 20 versions, with hide-and-check validation.
  Code only; no data. Version 1.0 is the code behind the Sage Research Methods case
  "Suppression Imputation and Joint Distributions With an AI Coding Agent".
repository-code: "https://github.com/lhao/InverseCSS"
keywords:
  - suppression imputation
  - raking
  - Dirichlet-multinomial
  - synthetic data
  - QCEW
  - QWI
